1.  **Function Signature (`pub fn factorial(n: u64) -> u64`)**:
    *   It takes one argument, `n`, which is of type `u64` (unsigned 64-bit integer). We use `u64` because factorials grow very quickly, and `u64` provides a large range (up to $20!$).
